{"id":5222,"date":"2021-04-13T13:26:48","date_gmt":"2021-04-13T12:26:48","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.eleanorgail.co.uk\/?p=5222"},"modified":"2021-04-13T13:37:32","modified_gmt":"2021-04-13T12:37:32","slug":"the-sequel-wedding-at-penrice-castle","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/eleanorgail.co.uk\/uncategorized\/the-sequel-wedding-at-penrice-castle\/","title":{"rendered":"The Sequel Wedding at Penrice Castle"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>One of the trends to come forward in this beautiful industry I work in is The Sequel Wedding. With wedding postponement\u2019s at an all-time high creating disappointment and uncertainty, couples are taking back control by saying \u201cI Do\u201d, embracing the intimate micro wedding and hosting a large celebration at a later date. I mean, who wouldn\u2019t want 2 celebrations and the perfect excuse to wear that stunning dress twice?! Sounds like a fabulous plan to me and I have clients doing exactly that.<\/p>\n<p>So what do you do when The Bride is originally from Quebec, The Groom from Mumbles and they\u2019re living in the US? The Sequel Wedding becomes a romantic wedding trilogy across 3 countries and set over snow (Quebec), sand (Massachusetts) and sea views (The Gower).<\/p>\n<p>Elaine and David needed a wedding planner with local knowledge to plan a wedding celebration for 50 guests in 4 weeks and we embraced the opportunity. With two other international and glamorous celebrations to live up to, only a unique venue steeped in centuries of Welsh history with fantastic sea views would do. So that&#8217;s what we did. And they married in the grounds of Penrice Castle with views over one of the most stunning costlines in the world.<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-5244\" src=\"https:\/\/www.eleanorgail.co.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/Elinor-Gail-Wedding-Owen-Mathias-Photography-ED-Penrice-WMd-07-Jul-1635-NIKON-D5398-6-scaled.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2560\" heigh